course: dictionary
lesson: 3048
title: Easily and its meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Easily is an adverb, a word that tells us how something is done or how likely it is. It has three main meanings, and the sentence around it shows which one you need. «She solved the puzzle easily» means she solved it without difficulty.
explain: «Glass breaks easily» means glass is quick to break, so it needs careful packing. When easily is about how likely something is, it means very likely. Look at what is happening in the sentence to choose the right meaning.
explain: «It is easily the best cake» means clearly the best, with no doubt at all. Easily can also be compared: more easily, most easily. Try your meaning in the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
fact: Easily is an adverb: it tells how, or how likely, something happens.
fact: «Easily» means without difficulty, as in «She solved the puzzle easily».
fact: «Easily» can mean very quickly or very likely, as in «Glass breaks easily».
fact: «Easily» can mean clearly, without doubt, as in «It is easily the best cake».
fact: «Gets upset easily» means is quick to be upset, and the comparative forms are more easily and most easily.
exercise: «She solved the puzzle easily.» What does easily mean here? | Far away | Only just, after a long fight | *Without difficulty | Very loudly
exercise: «Glass breaks easily, so pack it carefully.» What does easily mean here? | *Very quickly, or very likely, to break | Only just | Never, not at all | Without difficulty, so it is simple to lift
exercise: Dad says «It is easily the best cake I have ever had.» What does easily mean? | Very quickly | *Clearly, without any doubt | Without difficulty | Just a little bit
test: «The gritters spread salt, so ice forms less easily.» What does less easily mean here? | Only just | More quickly than before | Without any salt at all | *Less likely to form
test: Maya says «He gets upset easily.» What does this mean? | *He is quick to be upset | He is always happy | He never gets upset | He is upset, but only at night
exam: «Cold muscles strain more easily, so warm up slowly.» What does more easily mean? | Without difficulty at all, so no warm-up is needed | Clearly, without doubt | *More likely to strain | Only just
